            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0258" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/222</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Stevens [from Willard]:</p>
                <p>Your cable 16th instant.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d311-f1"/> Emerson sailed from San
                    Francisco November 18 with 350 men, including interpreters. Two hundred and
                    thirteen make up the instruction unit requested by Stevens. Remaining number
                    include interpreters and the mechanics that are being sent by Baldwin Locomotive
                    Co. to erect new engines at Vladivostok.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
